{
  "version": "2.0",
  "pipeline_stage": "validated",
  "title": "Sustained Attention Task (gradCPT) Dataset using simultaneous EEG-fMRI and DTI",
  "description": "This dataset comprises simultaneous EEG, fMRI, and diffusion-weighted imaging (DWI) recordings from 28 healthy adults performing a sustained attention gradual-onset continuous performance task (gradCPT), along with resting-state, checkerboard, and imagery task data. The dataset supports multimodal investigation of sustained attention and its neural correlates using combined electrophysiological, hemodynamic, and structural connectivity measures.",
  "methods_description": "Data were acquired using a 3T Siemens Magnetom Prisma MRI scanner for fMRI and DWI, and a 64-channel Brain Products BrainCap MR with Multirodes for simultaneous EEG recording. Tasks included resting state (eyes open and closed), a checkerboard visual stimulation task (15Hz), the gradCPT sustained attention task, and an imagery task.",
